    <string name="menu_pip_adb_title">Enable PiP via ADB</string>
    <string name="dialog_pip_adb_guide_title">Picture-in-Picture ADB Guide</string>
    <string name="dialog_pip_adb_guide_text"><![CDATA[
Some TV manufacturers block Picture-in-Picture (PiP) by default. Follow these steps to permanently enable it:<br><br>
1. Enable Developer Options on your TV (click "Build Number" 7 times in System Settings).<br>
2. Enable "ADB Debugging" inside Developer Options.<br>
3. Open a Command Prompt / Terminal on your PC and connect to your TV:<br>
<tt><b>adb connect [YOUR_TV_IP]:5555</b></tt><br><br>
4. Copy and execute the following commands exactly:<br>
<tt><b>adb shell appops set com.shipofagony.klippshell4creality PICTURE_IN_PICTURE allow</b></tt><br><br>
<tt><b>adb shell appops set com.shipofagony.klippshell4creality SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW allow</b></tt><br><br>
<tt><b>adb shell dumpsys deviceidle whitelist +com.shipofagony.klippshell4creality</b></tt><br><br>
5. Restart the KlippShell app on your TV. PiP is now permanently ready to use!<br><br>
Or simply use the KlippShellHelper extension:<br>
<tt>https://github.com/Ship-of-Agony/KlippShell-Helper</tt>
]]></string>

    <!-- BLOCK 12: SYSTEM-OVERLAY BERECHTIGUNGEN (PIP FALLBACK ERSTEINRICHTUNG) -->
    <string name="overlay_permission_title">Display Over Other Apps</string>
    <string name="overlay_permission_desc">Since some TV devices block native Picture-in-Picture (PiP), KlippShell requires this permission as a fallback. This allows the app to display a stable, floating mini-view over other TV apps (such as Netflix or Prime) so you can always keep an eye on your printer status while watching TV. Please enable KlippShell in the following system settings.</string>
    <string name="overlay_permission_btn">Enable Now</string>

