    <!-- BLOCK 19: WELCOME-TILE INITIAL INFORMATIONSCENTRUM -->
    <string name="welcome_tile_title">Welcome to KlippShell! 👋</string>
    <string name="welcome_tile_msg">Great to have you here! To help you get the most out of your printer monitoring, here is a quick overview of KlippShell\'s core features and the specifics of certain TV devices. KlippShell is designed to run smoothly on your smartphone, tablet, or Android TV.\n\n1️⃣ GETTING STARTED\nAdd your first 3D printer below. Almost all models currently on the market are included. If you use another Klipper-based printer, you can select \"Custom Printer\".\nNote: Depending on your printer model and network configuration, you may need to adjust your ports and camera URLs manually to ensure seamless monitoring. However, the automatic network scan should cover most setups on its own.\n⚠️ If you do not get a live image from your printer, please check out https://github.com/DnG-Crafts/K2-Camera and install the FIX. Unfortunately, this requires root access on the printer!\n💡 Tip: Long-pressing one of your saved printers in the main menu opens options to edit it, switch the default view between Live Stream monitoring and Klipper OS, or delete the printer.\n\n2️⃣ SMART LIVE CONTROLS\nIn video stream mode, you control everything using the three main buttons at the bottom:\n• Left button: Opens the menu for On-Screen Display (OSD), video zoom, PiP, enclosure lighting, screensaver, and aspect ratio.\n• Middle button: Seamlessly switches between Klipper OS (Dashboard) and the pure camera live stream.\n• Right button: Safely returns you to the main menu at any time.\n\n3️⃣ DIRECT START MODE\nOnce you have successfully configured a printer, you can enable Direct Start mode in the settings. This allows you to jump straight into your preferred printer view upon app launch.\n\n4️⃣ COMPANION MODE\nWith KlippShell, you can use your device as a TV dashboard (Master) or as a smartphone remote control (Slave). Enable Companion Mode in the settings to comfortably control your TV from your smartphone.\n\n5️⃣ PICTURE-IN-PICTURE (PiP)\nAlthough KlippShell fully supports PiP, some TV manufacturers restrict this feature natively. Don\'t worry: in the settings, you will find a guide explaining how to easily unlock PiP on your TV via an ADB command!\n\n6️⃣ TV \"NOW LIVE\" FUNCTION\nIf you want to use the \"Now Live\" TV channel feature, manufacturer restrictions may prevent it from showing up natively on your stock TV launcher. In this case, we recommend using an alternative TV launcher such as \"Projectivity Launcher\" on your TV device to enjoy this feature to the fullest.</string>
    <string name="welcome_tile_btn">Got It &amp; Hide</string>

